<!-- THE STORY -->
<section class="story-section" id="story">
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-label">The Story</div>
    <div class="story-grid">
      <div class="story-sidebar reveal">
        <p class="story-pull-quote">"Numbers without story are just spreadsheets — but numbers with narrative drive decisions."</p>
      </div>
      <div class="story-body reveal">
        <p>Before there was a finance team, there was a staff accountant closing the books alone at a veterinary startup that was growing faster than its infrastructure could handle. Christopher Keyser joined BetterVet when it was still figuring out what it wanted to be. Within four years, he helped answer that question.</p>
        <p>From supporting a $40M Series A to engineering the financial architecture that carried the company through acquisition, merger, and restructuring, Christopher became the person leadership turned to when the stakes were highest. When the CFO departed, the board chose not to hire above him. That decision told the full story.</p>
        <p>Today, as an Associate in Restructuring at G2 Capital Advisors, he advises middle-market companies navigating the same kind of inflection points he lived through firsthand. He builds models, sure. But more importantly, he builds clarity — translating financial complexity into the strategic insight that boards, lenders, and operators need to move forward with conviction.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
 
<!-- CAREER TIMELINE -->
<section class="timeline-section" id="career">
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-label">Career</div>
    <h2 class="section-headline">A progression built on<br>showing up when it matters</h2>
    <div class="timeline">
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-date">2026 — Present</div>
        <div class="timeline-role">Associate, Restructuring</div>
        <div class="timeline-company">G2 Capital Advisors · Boston</div>
        <div class="timeline-desc">Advising middle-market companies on turnaround strategy. Building integrated financial models, 13-week cash flow forecasts, and operating plans for clients navigating complex transitions.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-date">2025 — 2026</div>
        <div class="timeline-role">Finance Manager (FP&A & Operations)</div>
        <div class="timeline-company">The Vets · Boston</div>
        <div class="timeline-desc">Led the entire finance function post-merger, reporting directly to the CEO and Board. Orchestrated $30M+ in revenue oversight, built P&L frameworks across 27 cities, and drove a 50% margin improvement initiative. The board trusted the work enough to not hire a CFO.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-date">2024 — 2025</div>
        <div class="timeline-role">Assistant Controller</div>
        <div class="timeline-company">The Vets (post-acquisition) · Boston</div>
        <div class="timeline-desc">Integrated two ERP systems in 90 days, consolidated 12 legal entities, and migrated $15M in revenue recognition without material restatement. Designed the board reporting package from scratch.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-date">2022 — 2024</div>
        <div class="timeline-role">Senior Accountant → Assistant Controller</div>
        <div class="timeline-company">BetterVet (acquired by The Vets) · Boston</div>
        <div class="timeline-desc">Implemented Oracle NetSuite, supported the first institutional audit, and drove $300K in G&A savings. Scaled finance infrastructure from 6 to 20 locations. Managed a growing team and earned the trust of the C-Suite along the way.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-date">2021 — 2022</div>
        <div class="timeline-role">Staff Accountant</div>
        <div class="timeline-company">BetterVet · Boston</div>
        <div class="timeline-desc">The starting line. Executed month-end close across multiple entities, supported due diligence for a $40M Series A, and built the daily cash flow reporting that investors relied on every morning.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-date">2019 — 2022</div>
        <div class="timeline-role">Emmanuel College</div>
        <div class="timeline-company">B.A. Economics & Finance · Boston</div>
        <div class="timeline-desc">Technical Project Manager and Technology Associate. Managed a team of 8, led the campus through remote work transitions, and discovered that the intersection of systems and people was where the interesting work lived.</div>
      </div>
